\label{sec:hecke-algebras}

Let $\Gamma$ be a Dynkin diagram.  Attached to this Dynkin diagram, we have:
\begin{itemize}
\item An {\bf Artin braid group} $\Br_{\Gamma}$, which is generated by
  symbols $\si_i$ corresponding to vertices $i$ of $\Gamma$, with the relations
  \begin{equation*}
   \underbrace{\si_i\si_j\cdots}_{m_{ij} \text{ terms}}=\underbrace{\si_j\si_i\cdots}_{m_{ij} \text{ terms}}
  \end{equation*}
  where $m_{ij}$ is the Coxeter matrix:
  \begin{align*}
    m_{ij}=2&\quad \text{ if }\al_i^\vee(\al_j)\cdot\al_j^\vee(\al_i)=0, &
    m_{ij}=3&\quad \text{ if }\al_i^\vee(\al_j)\c
